From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:39:39 +0200
Subject: Video: fullscreen at the screen's size by default

On a console on a TV the game belongs fullscreen; a fresh configuration
started in a small window (the smoke run of 2026-10-19), because the
default was windowed and the size, when none was saved, the smallest mode
in the list. Now a fresh configuration is fullscreen at the desktop's
size, which SDL 1.2 reports before the first SetVideoMode (1920x1080 on
the PS3, through sdl12-compat). The Options menu and a saved config.xml
still change both.

Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/src/game/config.cpp b/src/game/config.cpp
--- a/src/game/config.cpp
+++ b/src/game/config.cpp
@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ Config::Config()
   , video_fullscreen(true) // No other mode supported
   , max_fps(25)
 #else
-  , video_fullscreen(false)
+  , video_fullscreen(true) // Walnut: a console on a TV
   , max_fps(50)
 #endif
 
diff --git a/src/graphic/video.cpp b/src/graphic/video.cpp
--- a/src/graphic/video.cpp
+++ b/src/graphic/video.cpp
@@ -70,8 +70,16 @@ Video::Video()
   int w = config->GetVideoWidth();
   int h = config->GetVideoHeight();
   if (!w || !h) {
-    w = available_configs.begin()->GetX();
-    h = available_configs.begin()->GetY();
+    // No size saved yet: the screen's own (SDL 1.2 reports the desktop's before the first
+    // SetVideoMode); the smallest mode, 640x480 or so, was the old choice
+    const SDL_VideoInfo *info = SDL_GetVideoInfo();
+    if (info && info->current_w >= 480 && info->current_h >= 320) {
+      w = info->current_w;
+      h = info->current_h;
+    } else {
+      w = available_configs.begin()->GetX();
+      h = available_configs.begin()->GetY();
+    }
   }
 
   SetConfig(w, h, config->IsVideoFullScreen());
